    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 one-antipodal packets have a collision-or-high-support dichotomy",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "Every complete one-antipodal c=2 packet either has four distinct barycentric weights and mismatch support at least 4H-2, or has exactly one equal weight pair and lies on the same two L/Q branches with the outer square-class gate. Thus every support at most 4H-4 is in the collision branch. Neither branch is excluded, and minimum-support-only gates are not extended.",
